="/encyclopedia/lozere"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lozere.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lozère</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Lozère is a department of southern France in the Occitanie region, created in 1790 largely from the former Gévaudan, with its prefecture at Mende.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lozi-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lozi people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Lozi, earlier called the Luyi or Aluyana, are a people of the upper Zambezi floodplain in western Zambia, whose kingdom of Barotseland was ruled by the Litunga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lu-bu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lu-bu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lü Bu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lü Bu was a Chinese warlord of the late Eastern Han dynasty, famed for his martial skill and notorious for betraying his patrons.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lu-buwei"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lu-buwei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lü Buwei</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lü Buwei was a wealthy merchant who became chancellor of the State of Qin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lu-guang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lu-guang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lü Guang</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lü Guang was a Di general of Former Qin whom the emperor Fu Jian sent to the Tarim Basin